    "big": "Rose black spot causes purple or black leaf spots. Leaves may yellow and drop early, reducing photosynthesis and growth. Fungal disease can spread through the environment in water or wind. Removing and destroying affected leaves and using fungicides can help control it.",
    "learn": [
      {
        "title": "Rose black spot is fungal",
        "text": "Rose black spot causes purple or black leaf spots. Leaves may yellow and drop early, reducing photosynthesis and growth. Fungal disease can spread through the environment in water or wind. Removing and destroying affected leaves and using fungicides can help control it.",
        "scene": "infection:leaf"
      },
      {
        "title": "The mosquito carries the pathogen",
        "text": "Malaria is caused by a protist. Its life cycle includes a mosquito, which acts as a vector: it carries the pathogen between hosts. Malaria causes recurrent episodes of fever and can be fatal. The mosquito itself is not the protist pathogen.",
        "scene": "infection:mosquito"
      },
      {
        "title": "Break the vector route",
        "text": "Reducing mosquito breeding lowers vector numbers. Nets help prevent mosquito bites. These measures interrupt different links in transmission; neither turns the mosquito into the pathogen or treats every existing human infection.",
        "scene": "infection:mosquito"
      }
    ],
